=== Bees ===
[[Bee]]s engage in a pollinating behavior with lilies of the valley, increasing the honey level in [[beehive]]s and [[bee nest]]s by 1.

=== Breeding ===
Lilies of the valley can be used to [[breed]], grow, and lead [[bee]]s.

=== Bee nests ===
[[Oak]], [[birch]], and [[cherry]] trees grown from [[sapling]]s that are within 2 blocks of a lily of the valley have a 5% chance to grow with a [[bee nest]] and 2-3 [[bee]]s in it.

=== Composting ===
Placing a lily of the valley into a [[composter]] has a 65% chance of raising the compost level by 1. A stack of lilies of the valley yields an average of 5.94 [[bone meal]].

